    "https://irp.cdn-website.com/62fe7d2a/files/uploaded/Biology+new+8.6.26.pdf": {
      "title": "Full-Time Position",
      "description": " \n \n \nFull-Time Position \nAssistant Professor of Biology \n \nUnion Commonwealth University invites applications for a full-time Assistant Professor of \nBiology beginning August 11, 2026. \nThe successful candidate will demonstrate a strong commitment to excellence in undergraduate \nteaching, student mentoring, academic advising, curriculum development, recruitment and \nretention, scholarly and professional development appropriate to the appointment, and service to \nthe Department, School, and University. \nApplicants from diverse academic and professional backgrounds are encouraged to apply, \nincluding those with expertise in the biological sciences, biomedical sciences, medicine, nursing, \nand other health-related disciplines. \nApplicants with an earned terminal degree (Ph.D. or equivalent) in Biology or a closely related \ndiscipline, as outlined in the Qualifications for Tenure-Track Appointment section below, are \neligible for appointment to a tenure-track position. Candidates with a master's degree in Biology \nor a related field may be considered for a full-time, non-tenure-track appointment. Additionally, \nindividuals with appropriate graduate credentials and substantial professional experience in a \nhealth-related discipline, including medicine, nursing, physician assistant studies, or allied \nhealth, who are academically qualified to teach biology courses, are encouraged to apply and \nmay also be considered for a full-time, non-tenure-track appointment. \nPosition Responsibilities \nThe successful candidate will: \n Teach undergraduate lecture and laboratory courses in biology based on departmental \nneeds and the candidate's areas of expertise. \n Teach foundational courses such as General Biology, Human Biology, Anatomy and \nPhysiology, Microbiology, Cell Biology, Genetics, Ecology, Evolution, and upper-level \nbiology courses as assigned. \n Develop engaging learning experiences that integrate scientific principles with practical \napplications and current biological research. \n Foster critical thinking, scientific inquiry, laboratory skills, and evidence-based decision \nmaking. \n Advise and mentor biology majors and students pursuing careers in healthcare, medicine, \nnursing, education, research, environmental sciences, and other life science professions. \n Participate in curriculum assessment, program development, student recruitment, and \nacademic advising. \n Contribute to departmental, university, and professional service activities. \n \n \n Maintain an active program of professional development, scholarship, research, or \nclinical practice appropriate to the discipline. \n Collaborate with faculty across academic programs to support interdisciplinary teaching \nand student success. \nRequired Qualifications \nApplicants must possess: \n An earned master's degree or higher in Biology, Biomedical Sciences, Medicine, Nursing \n(ARNP), Physiology, Microbiology, Genetics, Biochemistry, or another closely related \nlife science discipline by the time of appointment. \n Evidence of successful college-level teaching or demonstrated potential for excellence in \nundergraduate instruction. \n Ability to teach introductory biology and contribute across multiple areas of the \nundergraduate biology curriculum. \n Strong communication, organizational, and interpersonal skills. \n A commitment to student-centered learning, academic excellence, and faculty \ncollaboration. \nQualifications for Tenure-Track Appointment \nPreference will be given to candidates holding an earned terminal degree, including but not \nlimited to: \n Ph.D. in Biology or a related biological science \n Doctor of Medicine (MD) \n Doctor of Osteopathic Medicine (DO) \n Doctor of Nursing Practice (DNP) \n Other appropriate earned doctoral degree in a closely related discipline \nCandidates who are ABD or nearing completion of a terminal degree may be considered, with \nappointment status determined according to university policies. \nAdditional preferred qualifications include: \n Experience teaching undergraduate laboratory courses. \n Clinical experience as a physician (MD or DO), advanced practice registered nurse \n(APRN), nurse practitioner, physician assistant, or other healthcare professional. \n Experience mentoring undergraduate research, internships, or experiential learning. \n Commitment to active-learning strategies and innovative instructional methods. \n Interest in interdisciplinary collaboration with programs such as Nursing, Exercise \nScience, Psychology, Education, Chemistry, and Environmental Science. \n Demonstrated commitment to student success, mentorship, and community engagement. \n \n \n \n \nAbout Union Commonwealth University \nUnion Commonwealth University is a private, liberal arts institution located in Barbourville, \nKentucky, with a longstanding commitment to educating students for meaningful lives and \ncareers. Founded in the Appalachian region, Union combines personalized education with \nopportunities for students to engage deeply with their communities and the wider world. Our \nfaculty are dedicated teachers, mentors, and scholars who value close student relationships, \nclassroom innovation, and the transformative power of higher education.  \nApplication Process \nApplicants should submit: \n Letter of application addressing qualifications and interest in the position \n Curriculum vitae \n Statement of teaching philosophy \n Unofficial transcripts (official transcripts required upon appointment) \n Contact information for three professional references \nApplications will be reviewed immediately and will continue until the position is filled. \nUnion Commonwealth University (the \"University\") is committed to maintaining an educational, \nemployment, and business environment free of all forms of discrimination. The University \nprovides full and equal access to its educational services, classes, and programs without regard to \nand prohibits discrimination based on the protected characteristics of age (40 and older), race, \ncolor, national origin, ancestry, religion, sex (including transgender status, gender identity or \nexpression), pregnancy (including childbirth, lactation, and related medical conditions), physical \nor mental disability, AIDS/HIV status, genetic information (including testing and \ncharacteristics), veteran status, uniformed servicemember status, status as a smoker or \nnonsmoker, medical condition, sexual orientation, marital status, or because an individual is \nperceived to have one or more of the foregoing characteristics, or any other status protected by \nfederal, state, or local laws. \n "
    }
  },
